  "name": "Desgarrada minhota (Minho sung challenge)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Cantares ao desafio, also called desgarrada, are the sung verse challenges of the Minho and neighbouring northern Portugal, in which two or more cantadores, very often a man and a woman, improvise alternating quatrains of teasing, argument and flirtation at fairs, romarias and village festivals. A concertina, in Portugal a diatonic button accordion, usually carries the repeated tune and interludes, sometimes with a triangle (ferrinhos), and northern cantadores have issued desgarradas on commercial cassettes and CDs since the late twentieth century; the accordion card stands for the concertina.",
